<h1>Connie Anderson</h1>
<p>Chicago Board of Education, District 10b, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Incumbent. Endorsed by the Chicago Teachers Union.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>According to the candidate platform text published on the Chicago Teachers Union&#39;s 2026 election page, Anderson says she is running to fight for fully funded schools, including full funding and staffing for special education services, hands-on job training and career and technical education classes, art and music programming that celebrates culture and community, and healthy, safe, and modern school facilities.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Mother of CPS graduates, award-winning school robotics team coach, and co-owner of the Record Track in South Chicago; spent 12 years with the Friends of Ogden parent group and was involved in the 2018 Ogden-Jenner school merger. Appointed to the board by Mayor Brandon Johnson in July 2026 to fill the District 10b vacancy.</p>
